 a  message  now i'm shooting this video in part as  an update because i'm sure you know i've  got something like four thousand odd  viewers at this point  and most of them have uh  four thousand subscribers most of them  have no idea you know what happened with  my lag  or anything like that i have a facebook  page and the people who who consult that  they've known about why i haven't been  doing very much for the last week  for a while but i didn't put any  announcement on on youtube perhaps i  should have  since i know people look forward to  these these videos  in any case um  you can expect to see some more personal  videos coming out if that's not your  thing maybe you know tune out for a  little while and wait until i start  talking about aristotle and plato and  augustine and that sort of thing again  but if that is the sort of thing that  you're interested in um you could stay  tuned so  let me think if there's anything else to  tell you about oh yeah so so the uh the  injury  it was really kind of strange  we were we were in the surf and it was  high tide  and um kind of an overcast day i'm gonna  be actually shooting another video or  putting together another video some of  the shots that i got that day some  beautiful shots of the ocean  and you know the waves were rolling in  we were trying to to wash off the sand  from our bodies because we'd done the  thing where each one of us you know got  buried up to our our head of the sand  but then there's lots of sand on us and  we're getting ready to pack up  so i was out in the  the waves and they didn't seem like they  were that high but you know i turned my  attention away  from the waves for for just you know  short short period of time  and i got i got washed over  and hit by them  and i went down and  i'm not sure exactly what happened i  know that as i was coming up it could be  that you know current was pulling  one way or pushing one way or something  like that and that my foot landed in the  wrong way but i felt something given my  my knee now when you're a guy in your  40s that's definitely not something that  you want to feel i mean it hurt to begin  with  but it's interesting because  it was it was scary not because of the  pain i mean i've felt much worse pain  before  different injuries and things like that  burns in particular  but um it was scary because i could you  could feel this you know you could feel  the knee joint slipping or giving or  something like that and you know that  something like that is a bad injury  so  that's um  that's what was going on i got myself  out of the the surf because you know i'm  strong enough with my arms to like you  know pull myself  but my my my knee was basically useless  i tried to get up and put weight on it  and it just crumpled up and again it was  painful but it was it was scarier  because of the way it just sort of  gave out  so i had to  get myself out of the surf luckily my my  wife was close by and she could help you  know get me out  and then it was a question of getting me  back up to you know where the uh the  towels and all of our our gear was so we  could start thinking about what's going  on what are we going to do  and  i i got to say everybody at montauk was  was really helpful  you know the first responders um the  people at the hotel that we were staying  helped out  and uh they were very generous actually  they they switched our rooms so we could  stay in a  lower room  so i wouldn't have to go up the stairs  because by then it was starting to to by  the time that i got back from the  hospital was starting to hurt  so you know  it was pretty clear i had to go to the  hospital and we got we got me off the  beach  or rather they got me off the beach  and  got me into an ambulance and the whole  time  it really wasn't hurting that bad  unless i did certain things  and i was more worried about whether i  damaged anything within the knee whether  it was going to be one of those sort of  cases where  